# Module: ingestion_worker (Phase 1)
Compile unit for the Orchestration Service. **Called by `ingestion_service`** (the daemon owns the `BRPOP` loop, idempotency, and dead-letter; this module is the pure screening step it invokes per batch).
Generates: `orchestrator/ingestion_worker.py`

## Role
Safety + relevancy + coherence screening of one already-dequeued batch. The only module that ever reads raw, unscreened payload content. Exposes `screen_batch(batch) -> survivors` — it does **not** own the queue loop.

## Behavior (given a parsed batch envelope)
1. Build the **App Identity Digest**: the `# Role and Purpose` and core-feature summary of the target prompt file — its path resolved from the `TARGET_PROMPT_DIR` env var (`${TARGET_PROMPT_DIR}/streaks_demo_typescriptreact.prompt`; never hardcode the directory) — kept under ~150 tokens.
2. Call `llm_client.call_agent("security_relevance_gatekeeper", ...)` with the digest and the batch. Treat the verdict as content policy — the backend already validated payload shape.
3. Dropped features (MALICIOUS, OFF_TOPIC, or UNCLEAR — title/description plainly incoherent) are never persisted anywhere: call `telemetry.publish_screening_result(feature_id, author_id, reason)` for each (reason category `security` | `off_topic` | `unclear` — never the content) and `telemetry.log_decision(...)` with a content-free entry (feature_id, classification, reason category, model version only).
4. Call `telemetry.publish_agent_event(phase="screening", ...)` once per batch with human-readable copy (aggregate counts only, e.g., "🛡️ Guardagent is screening 14 new feature requests..."); never echo dropped content.
5. **Read quarantine**: return only the survivor set to the caller (`ingestion_service`, which hands it to `pm_agent`); raw batch content never leaves this module.

## Error handling (fail-closed — the caller owns redelivery)
- **Fail-closed**: on any screening failure — `AgentResponseError` (malformed after one corrective retry), `AgentRefusalError` (model declined — no retry), or exhausted `LLMTransientError` — **do not return survivors; raise so the batch is dropped/held, never default-passed.** Unscreened content must not reach the feed because a verdict couldn't be obtained. Write a **content-free** `decision_log` entry (batch_id, phase, failure class, model version — never the pitch text) before raising.
- The **bounded redelivery + dead-letter** decision (whether a raised failure is redelivered or moved to `failed_intake:{batch_id}`) belongs to `ingestion_service`, which owns `intake_attempts:{batch_id}`, `processed_batches`, and the `BRPOP` loop. This module only guarantees it never silently passes an unscreened batch.

